These are the steps in building a jar file from the intellij.

Steps:
1. Open the terminal and run this command:
javac -d out src/prototype/tiffany_lau_kho_jen/*.java

2. Now, I copy my ‘pictures’ folder from the src into the out/ directory.

3. I create a file named MANIFEST.MF in the same folder as the src and out.

The content of the MANIFEST.MF would be:
Manifest-Version: 1.0
Main-Class: prototype.tiffany_lau_kho_jen.Main

4. Then, in the terminal I enter the full path to jar.exe like this:
& "C:\Program Files\Java\jdk-21\bin\jar.exe" cfm Game.jar MANIFEST.MF -C out .

5. Then, you can test the JAR using: java -jar Game.jar


Now these are the steps to create the executable file (.exe) from the JAR file.

1. Use Launch4j and for the output file, enter Santorini.exe.

2. For the jar, select the Game.jar that is just created from the “Jar” section

3. Build the generated file named Santorini.exe by pressing the ‘gear’ button.

4. Test the exe file by pressing the triangular button at the top left.


